{"name":"Desert Sunrise","hex":"#fcb58d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"desert","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A barren area of land or desolate terrain, especially one with little water or vegetation; a wasteland.\n\nIn particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground.","In particular, a barren, arid area of land which is hot, with sandy, rocky, or parched ground."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Usually of a place: abandoned, deserted, or uninhabited."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/desert"},{"term":"sunrise","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time of day when the sun appears above the eastern horizon.","The change in color of the sky at dawn."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To phase in.","To awake."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunrise"}],"entries":[{"title":"Desert","blocks":[{"text":"A desert is a landscape where little precipitation occurs and, consequently, living conditions create unique biomes and ecosystems. The lack of vegetation exposes the unprotected surface of the ground to denudation. About one-third of the land surface of the Earth is arid or semi-arid. This includes much of the polar regions, where little precipitation occurs, and which are sometimes called polar deserts or \"cold deserts\". Deserts can be classified by the amount of precipitation that falls, by the temperature that prevails, by the causes of desertification or by their geographical location."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG/330px-Rub_al_Khali_002.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert","wikidata":"Q8514"},{"title":"Sunrise","blocks":[{"text":"Sunrise is the moment when the upper rim of the Sun appears on the horizon in the morning, at the start of the Sun path. The term can also refer to the entire process of the solar disk crossing the horizon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunrise","wikidata":"Q193294"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)","wikidata":"Q9303163"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/500px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/1280px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg/500px-Groupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A camel shepherd in southern Tunisia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGroupe_de_dromadaire_avec_son_chamelier_dans_le_sud_tunisien.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Deserts.png/500px-Desert